<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55942" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατηρεφής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρέφω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>covered over, vaulted, overhanging</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπέος εὺρὺ κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					13.349
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλισίας τε κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					18.589
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν σμήνεσσι κ. μέλισσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					594
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέγα κῦμα . . κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.367
				</span></i>
			: c. dat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπέος δάφνῃσι κ.</span>
			<i>shaded by, embowered in</i> them, <i><span class="en">
				9.183
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δώματα πέτρῃσι κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					778
				</span></i>
			; so in Trag., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. πέτρος</span>, of
			a cave, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				272
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν κ. στέγῃ χθονός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>El.</u>
					381
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. τύμβος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					885
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. αὐτῇ τῇ πέτρᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Criti.</u>
					116b
				</span></i>
			; of trees, <i>thick-leaved</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				7.9
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. πόδα τιθέναι</span> keep the
			foot <i>covered</i>, of Pallas seated, when the robe falls over
			her feet, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθὸν πόδα τ.</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				294
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέγην, ἧς κατηρεφεῖς δόμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					468
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τράπεζαι κ. παντοίων ἀγαθῶν</span>
			<i>covered with, full of</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anacr.
				121
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
